        </ul>

        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Streaks are differences in film thickness. Nearly all of them trace to an unstirred pail, a squeegee pushed too far, or sealer that flashed in the sun before it could level. Every one of those is fixed by a full-strength, properly mixed second coat applied crosswise on a cool morning.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Give faint streaks a month to weather out before you act. Recoat the crisp ones. Strip only when what is underneath is failing, because more sealer on a bad base is just more sealer to peel.
          </p>
        </div>

